+## HTTP admission discovery
+
+The subsequent [real-HTTP gateway comparison](evidence/performance-2026-10-24/bff-http-admission-discovery/README.md) preserves the increment-11 application, 100-account mixed workload, real session/RLS checks and five total BFF connections. Both variants accept all 600 first intentions and preserve every receipt, original history/XP and final shared snapshot; exact fixture cleanup passes. Least-pending request routing still fails with personal/shared scheduled p95 1,637.4/1,204.6 ms and one late observation. Serial admission through a bounded FIFO queue worsens those values to 7,123.1/6,627.9 ms and 26 late observations. All 200 shared updates are eventually observed in both runs.
+
+No runtime is adopted. Profile gateway wait, worker service, database acquisition/query, domain CPU and transport phases before another full routing change. Keep physical source-IP quotas, header/body/deadline handling, worker failure/restart and lost-response replay as runtime acceptance requirements. These gateways omit trusted peer/IP transport and are diagnostic only. A shorter group polling cadence may provide convergence headroom, but needs its own increased-read-load check. The current cadence and normal entry point remain unchanged.
